values ('f1a2b3c4-5d6e-4f16-9a85-9b0c1d2e3f06', 'hospitality-managerial-accounting', 'Hospitality Managerial Accounting', 'This course equips hospitality managers to plan, control, evaluate, and improve hotel, restaurant, resort, club, event, and multi-unit performance using financial and nonfinancial information. Students build contribution and CVP models, operating budgets and forecasts, flexible budgets and variance analyses, food/beverage and labor controls, departmental statements, relevant-cost decision models, pricing and profitability analyses, performance dashboards, and capital-investment cases. U.S. practice is emphasized through USALI 12th Revised Edition, restaurant account structures, IMA ethics, COSO-informed controls, and auditable spreadsheet discipline.');

